🛡️ AutoVulnScanner
An automated vulnerability scanning and reporting tool for web applications and networks. It generates PDF, JSON, and CSV reports based on scan results using OWASP ZAP and Nmap.

🔧 Features
Web vulnerability scanning (via OWASP ZAP)

Network vulnerability scanning (via Nmap)

Report generation (PDF, JSON, CSV)

Web-based dashboard interface using Flask

📁 Project Structure
graphql
Copy
Edit
project/
│
├── main.py               # Entry point for running the dashboard
├── config.json           # (Optional) Configuration file
├── templates/            # HTML templates for dashboard
├── static/               # Static files (CSS, JS)
├── reports/              # Generated scan reports
├── venv/                 # Virtual environment
└── README.md
🧰 Prerequisites
Python 3.10+

pip (Python package manager)

OWASP ZAP (must be running)

Nmap (for network scanning)

🔌 Installation
1. Clone the Repo
bash
Copy
Edit
git clone https://github.com/Ajithvenkat-10/AutoVulnScanner.git
cd AutoVulnScanner
If you face a 403 error, ensure that you're logged in as the right user or SSH is used for pushing.

2. Setup Virtual Environment
bash
Copy
Edit
python -m venv venv
venv\Scripts\activate  # On Windows
# OR
source venv/bin/activate  # On macOS/Linux
3. Install Dependencies
bash
Copy
Edit
pip install -r requirements.txt
If requirements.txt is missing, regenerate it with:

bash
Copy
Edit
pip freeze > requirements.txt
🚀 Running the Tool
1. Start OWASP ZAP
Ensure ZAP is running in the background. You can start it manually or in headless mode:

bash
Copy
Edit
"C:\Program Files\OWASP\Zed Attack Proxy\zap.bat"
Or for headless automation:

bash
Copy
Edit
zap.sh -daemon -port 8090 -host 127.0.0.1
2. Run the Flask Dashboard
bash
Copy
Edit
python main.py dashboard --port 5000
Access it at: http://127.0.0.1:5000

🌐 Web Interface
Enter the target URL

Choose Web Scan or Network Scan

Wait for the scan to complete

Download PDF/JSON/CSV reports from the reports/ folder

🧪 Troubleshooting
❗ ZAP not connected? Ensure it is running and accessible at the configured port (default: 8090)

❗ Nmap not found? Download and install from https://nmap.org/download.html and add to system PATH

❗ 403 Git error? Your Git credentials might belong to another user (Sne-V). Re-authenticate with your GitHub account:

bash
Copy
Edit
git remote set-url origin https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/AutoVulnScanner.git
git config --global credential.helper manager-core
